course: dictionary
lesson: 13761
title: A formal word: interposition
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Interposition is a long, formal word. You will meet it most in old books, legal writing and science. Break it apart: inter means between, and position means place. So interposition means putting something in between, or stepping in between.
explain: «The interposition of a cloud made the field go dark.» The cloud came between the sun and the field, and the field went dark. So interposition means something coming between two things.
explain: The second meaning is about people. «Her calm interposition stopped the two boys from fighting.» She stepped in between them to stop what was happening. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "her calm stepping in between them stopped the fight" still makes sense.
explain: Artists and scientists use the idea too. When a tree hides part of a house, the tree is in between you and the house. The hidden house looks further away, so interposition helps us judge depth.
fact: Interposition means putting something between two things, or stepping in between people to stop or change what is happening.
fact: Inter means between, and position means place, so the word is about getting into the middle.
fact: «Interposition» is a formal word: you will meet it most in old books, legal writing and science.
fact: In art and science, interposition is a depth clue: when one object hides part of another, the hidden one looks further away.
fact: Two phrases to know: «by interposition» and «the interposition of». Both are about something being put between, or coming between, two things.
exercise: «The interposition of a cloud made the field go dark.» What does interposition mean here? | A kind of farm animal | A loud noise from the sky | A cloud that is very big and white | *Something coming between the sun and the field
exercise: «Her calm interposition stopped the two boys from fighting.» What did she do? | She gave them both a prize | She joined in the fight | *She stepped in between them to stop the fight | She ran away from the boys
exercise: In a drawing, a tree hides part of a house. Which one looks further away? | The sky, because it is high up | *The house, because the tree is in front of it | The tree, because it is hidden | Both look the same distance away
test:
Inter means between and position means place. What does interposition mean? | *Putting something between two things | Putting something on top of a table | Being very quiet | Running away from danger
test:
«The referee's interposition ended the argument between the two teams.» What does the referee's interposition mean? | *The referee stepped in between them to stop the argument | The referee sang a song to the crowd | The referee left the field early | The referee scored a goal
exam: «The interposition of his hand stopped the sun from dazzling his eyes.» What did his hand do? | It wiped the sweat from his face | *It came between the sun and his eyes | It made the sun shine brighter | It held his book steady
